3174 - &nbsp; Print &amp; Audio&nbsp;Manager

Overview of role&nbsp; &nbsp;

EssenceMediaCom handles the media planning and buying for some of the world's smartest advertisers.&nbsp; Supported by consumer insight, analysis and experience, we are part of the largest media planning and buying network in the world. &nbsp;

&nbsp; We are the only agency to simultaneously hold the title of Agency Network of the Year across all 5 of the industry’s biggest awards, whilst recently being named Campaign’s Media Agency of the Decade.&nbsp; &nbsp;

We are looking for a diligent&nbsp;Print and Audio&nbsp;Manager&nbsp;with at&nbsp;least&nbsp;two years of&nbsp;experience to work&nbsp;in the&nbsp;offline&nbsp;team.&nbsp;Clients include but are not limited to&nbsp;Boots,&nbsp;TUI&nbsp;and&nbsp;Costa.&nbsp;In this role you will&nbsp;be responsible for&nbsp;the entire planning&nbsp;and buying&nbsp;process, where you will make a recommendation to the client founded in insight and evidence, with audit guarantees in mind, before&nbsp;purchasing&nbsp;the inventory. &nbsp;

Ideally&nbsp;we would like to see&nbsp;some form of&nbsp;knowledge across&nbsp;print and/or&nbsp;audio. This is to ensure you&nbsp;have a foundation to build on. &nbsp;

&nbsp;

Reporting of the role &nbsp;

This role reports directly into the&nbsp;Associate Director&nbsp;on the account, along with the relevant&nbsp;people&nbsp;regarding value management, quality and channel coordination. &nbsp;

3 best things about the job &nbsp;

• EssenceMediaCom’s strength has always been our people. This team really reflects that. We’re a tight team working to deliver great&nbsp;insight-led work to our clients. &nbsp;

• A widely varied client base makes for a great place to grow your career as it gives everyone in the team a real breadth of experience. &nbsp;

• Exposure not only to planning of all&nbsp;print and audio, but the digital specialists in response to briefs, where we make a&nbsp;joined-up&nbsp;media recommendation across all channels.&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;

Measures of success

In three months, you would have:&nbsp; &nbsp;

• Learnt how to use all the key&nbsp;Print + Audio&nbsp;buying tools.&nbsp; &nbsp;

• Built a strong working relationship with the other individuals within Planning and Investment, as well as media owners externally.&nbsp; &nbsp;

• Developed a full understanding of the marketplace. &nbsp;

• Gained a good understanding of the client businesses which you will oversee. &nbsp;

&nbsp;

In six months, you would have: &nbsp;

• Developed strong Print + Audio planning skills &nbsp;

• A good understanding of Mediacom’s planning tools and data points and be able use them effectively to build rationale &nbsp;

• Worked in a multi-media team to deliver connected responses and present back to the client &nbsp;

&nbsp;

In 12 months, you would have: &nbsp;

• Responsibility and autonomy to deliver Print + Audio responses on your clients with minimal involvement from your AD. &nbsp;

• Developed strong client relationships and attend external meetings without more senior presence &nbsp;

• Have a good understanding of other media and the role of Print &amp; Audio in the connected system &nbsp;

