Infingame is an iGaming aggregator that gives online casino operators a single point of access to a broad range of games and gaming services, connecting them with more than 200 content suppliers worldwide. Built with performance and stability at its core, our platform delivers fast spin times and reliable connections across global markets - making us a trusted partner for operators with international ambitions.

Recognized within the gaming industry, including a shortlist for “Aggregator of the Year” at the SiGMA World Balkans & CIS Awards, we focus on building stable, flexible infrastructure that supports long-term growth for our partners, regardless of their scale or market.

As a Infingame team, we’re building technology our partners trust - and a company where people have the freedom to grow, take ownership, and make an impact.

Now we’re looking for a Senior DevOps Engineer to become а part of that journey.
Maybe that’s you?

Skills & experience that matter:
- 5+ years of experience working as a DevOps or Site Reliability Engineer (SRE);
- Strong hands-on experience with Kubernetes (AWS EKS preferred);
- Strong experience designing and operating production infrastructure on AWS;
- Experience designing and maintaining CI/CD pipelines using GitHub Actions;
- Strong experience with Terraform and Infrastructure as Code best practices;
- Experience with monitoring and observability tools (Prometheus, Grafana, ELK);
- Solid understanding of networking fundamentals (TCP/IP, DNS, HTTP/TLS, Load Balancing);
- Strong analytical and troubleshooting skills with attention to detail;
- Good communication skills and ability to work collaboratively as a team player.

Nice to have:
- Experience with GitOps (Argo CD is a plus);
- Python or Go scripting skills;
- Experience operating high-load distributed systems.

What you’ll do:
- Maintain and improve production and staging infrastructure;
- Support and develop CI/CD processes;
- Develop and improve Infrastructure as Code using Terraform;
- Investigate and troubleshoot issues;
- Improve observability, monitoring, and logging systems;
- Monitor production systems and respond to infrastructure incidents;
- Collaborate closely with software engineers;
- Maintain infrastructure documentation and operational runbooks.

Why Infingame ?

•
We work where feel most productive. Work remotely from anywhere in the world, or join us in a hybrid format if you’re based in Bratislava. We believe flexibility helps people do their best work.

•
We invest in people who want to grow. We already offer English and Slovak lessons, professional courses, and the support to keep learning and growing. If you’re ready to grow, we’ll invest in your development.

•
We believe good work starts with good rest. Enjoy 21 paid vacation days and additional public holidays based on the Ukrainian or Slovak calendar. We encourage everyone to take the time they need to switch off and recharge.

•
We look after our people. Health insurance in Ukraine and abroad, paid sick leave, and access to a corporate psychologist to help you take care of yourself.

•
We keep things simple. No unnecessary bureaucracy, no complicated hierarchies - just open communication and a team that’s easy to work with.

•
We make time to get together. From international exhibitions and conferences to company trips, team events, and online activities, we create plenty of opportunities to learn, celebrate, and spend time together.

What we stand for
Our culture is built on trust, collaboration, and ownership. We encourage people to take initiative, share ideas openly, support one another, and grow together. Everyone has a voice, and every contribution matters.

Ready to join us?
The next chapter of your career could start here - let’s build it together.
If you’re interested, send us your CV. All applications are treated with strict confidentiality, and only shortlisted candidates will be contacted.

